  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25145752",
      "title": "Dynamic Pages & \"getServerSideProps\"",
      "lectureOrder": 284,
      "videoOrder": 265,
      "sourceHash": "cc8849d8f0c2f889ceebd14e62151e9ae83f274d5a58af801f6892d1de895eeb",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.16,
          "end": 3.64,
          "en": "Now getServiceSideProps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.64,
          "end": 5.45,
          "en": "can sometimes be useful.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.45,
          "end": 8.01,
          "en": "I also want to mention how you would use it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.01,
          "end": 10.01,
          "en": "with a dynamic page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.01,
          "end": 13.85,
          "en": "Here before, when we used getStaticProps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.85,
          "end": 16.34,
          "en": "we also needed getStaticPaths",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.34,
          "end": 20.81,
          "en": "to let Next.js know which instances of this page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.81,
          "end": 23.26,
          "en": "should be pre-generated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.26,
          "end": 27.32,
          "en": "Now when using getServiceSideProps, that's not the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.32,
          "end": 32.32,
          "en": "If I do have a [Uid].js file, Uid in square brackets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.62,
          "end": 36.97,
          "en": "so that I have a dynamic page for a single user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.97,
          "end": 38.93,
          "en": "for different user IDs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.93,
          "end": 43.02,
          "en": "If we use getServiceSideProps we don't need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.02,
          "end": 45.423,
          "en": "and we can't use getStaticPaths.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.7,
          "end": 49.1,
          "en": "So here, if I have the UserIdPage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.35,
          "end": 52.2,
          "en": "and I get some props here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.2,
          "end": 57.093,
          "en": "and here I then simply return h1 tag where I put props,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 58.04,
          "end": 61.663,
          "en": "id something like this, and we then export this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 62.85,
          "end": 64.1,
          "en": "If we do all of that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.1,
          "end": 69.1,
          "en": "and I then also have this async getServerSideProps function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 70.83,
          "end": 71.993,
          "en": "which we export.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 72.85,
          "end": 75.08,
          "en": "If we have this, then you will see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 75.08,
          "end": 77.93,
          "en": "that we don't need getStaticPaths at all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 77.93,
          "end": 80.22,
          "en": "Here I just returned an object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 80.22,
          "end": 83.05,
          "en": "and now I'm interested in the concrete param value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 83.05,
          "end": 84.78,
          "en": "which I'm getting here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84.78,
          "end": 87.89,
          "en": "So we can get access to that through context.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 87.89,
          "end": 91.61,
          "en": "From there we can still extract params as I mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 91.61,
          "end": 94.84,
          "en": "and from params we can still get our userId",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.84,
          "end": 99.41,
          "en": "by accessing uid, since that's the identifier I picked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 99.41,
          "end": 101.62,
          "en": "between square brackets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 101.62,
          "end": 103.42,
          "en": "And then in the props which we passed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 103.42,
          "end": 105.42,
          "en": "to the component function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 105.42,
          "end": 109.22999999999999,
          "en": "we could have the id prop, since I'm accessing that here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 109.22999999999999,
          "end": 111.447,
          "en": "and set this equal to userid-",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 113.95,
          "end": 118.95,
          "en": "and then let's say the userId we extracted from the URL,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 119.00999999999999,
          "end": 122.25,
          "en": "just to have some dummy code here that proves",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 122.25,
          "end": 124.68,
          "en": "that this code actually did execute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 124.68,
          "end": 127.72,
          "en": "before this component function code ran.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 127.72,
          "end": 130.02,
          "en": "With that if you wanna test this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 130.02,
          "end": 133.57,
          "en": "we first of all need to make sure we get rid of [pid].js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 133.57,
          "end": 138.05,
          "en": "because otherwise we have two dynamic segment pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 138.05,
          "end": 141.02,
          "en": "on the same level in our pages folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 141.02,
          "end": 145.57,
          "en": "so Next.js wouldn't know if a value after slash",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 145.57,
          "end": 148.88,
          "en": "nothing should be a product ID or a user ID,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 148.88,
          "end": 153.03,
          "en": "and therefore if I move to pitfall",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 153.03,
          "end": 154.953,
          "en": "into the products folder here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 156.63,
          "end": 159.71,
          "en": "And in index.js I update my links",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 159.71,
          "end": 163.99,
          "en": "to go to /products/some ID,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 163.99,
          "end": 167.38,
          "en": "now we resolve the disc clash because now we know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 167.38,
          "end": 170.89,
          "en": "that if it's just slash something unrecognized,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 170.89,
          "end": 174.41,
          "en": "it will always target this user ID route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 174.41,
          "end": 178.74,
          "en": "And now with that, if I bring back that development server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 178.74,
          "end": 183.74,
          "en": "if we visit let's say /u1 for user one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 184.58,
          "end": 188.62,
          "en": "we see userid-u1 here so it worked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 188.62,
          "end": 193.62,
          "en": "And it did work without us adding getStaticPaths.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 193.89,
          "end": 198.31,
          "en": "Why? Because this runs on the server only anyways.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 198.31,
          "end": 202.5,
          "en": "So Next.js does not pre generate any pages at all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 202.5,
          "end": 205.2,
          "en": "and therefore of course, it also doesn't need to know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 205.2,
          "end": 207.63,
          "en": "which pages to pre-generate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 207.63,
          "end": 210.59,
          "en": "because there is no pre-generation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 210.59,
          "end": 213.62,
          "en": "So unlike in the other case with getStaticProps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 214.57999999999998,
          "end": 217.17000000000002,
          "en": "where we do pre-generate pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 217.17000000000002,
          "end": 220.89,
          "en": "and where we therefore for do need to tell Next.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 220.89,
          "end": 224.95,
          "en": "for which param values pages should be pre-generated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 224.95,
          "end": 228.89,
          "en": "with getServiceSideProps that's simply not an issue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 228.89,
          "end": 231.52,
          "en": "because we run that server side code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 231.52,
          "end": 234.02,
          "en": "for every request anyways.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 234.02,
          "end": 235.73,
          "en": "So there is no pre-generation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 235.73,
          "end": 238.96,
          "en": "and therefore no need to define those dynamic paths",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 238.96,
          "end": 240.68,
          "en": "in advance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 240.68,
          "end": 242.403,
          "en": "I hope that makes sense.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
